WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:04.650
From more superhero movies to down-to-earth
dramas and everything in between, here are

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:08.120
all the movies that are set to blow you away
in summer of 2019.

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:13.651
Kicking off summer on May 31 is Godzilla:
King of the Monsters, the follow-up to the

00:00:13.651 --> 00:00:18.609
well-received 2014 movie about the legendary
kaiju. The movie is the third installment

00:00:18.609 --> 00:00:23.640
in Legendary Entertainment's MonsterVerse,
following up on 2017's Kong: Skull Island

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:28.760
and setting up an eventual battle between
the two monsters in 2020's Godzilla vs. Kong.

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:31.540
"This island is just the beginning."

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:32.860
"There's more out there."

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:34.620
"What do you mean, more?"

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:37.560
"This world never belonged to us. It belonged
to them."

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:41.980
Hopefully that movie can live up to what we
got the last time Godzilla and King Kong threw

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:42.480
down:

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:56.120
On top of bringing back characters from the
2014 Godzilla, the sequel is bringing in a

00:00:56.120 --> 00:01:01.470
roster of fan favorite actors, including Stranger
Things' Millie Bobby Brown, Bates Motel's

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:06.440
Vera Farmiga, and Friday Night Lights' Kyle
Chandler. Together, they play a family swept

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:10.610
up in the crisis that the monsters of the
title cause, adding a human element to what

00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:13.240
promises to be a larger-than-life slugfest.

00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:18.870
Also coming out on June 7 is Long Shot, a
big-screen comedy team-up starring Seth Rogen

00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:23.470
and Charlize Theron. It comes from a script
by The Interview writer Dan Sterling, which

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:27.440
made the Black List collection of hottest
unproduced screenplays in 2011.

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:32.100
The movie stars Rogen as an out of work journalist
named Fred Flarsky who, after getting fed

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:35.920
up with his bad luck and self-destructive
ways, decides he's going to finally pursue

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:41.760
his longtime crush: a former babysitter from
his childhood. The only problem? She's since

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:46.460
become one of the most powerful women in the
world, as well as a presidential candidate.

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:50.920
Will he succeed in winning her affections?
We don't know, but it'll probably be funny

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:51.620
to see him try.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:57.900
Sony is bringing back the Men in Black series
with a new spinoff on June 14. The latest

00:01:57.909 --> 00:02:02.030
take on the comic book adaptation will take
the series beyond the bounds of New York City,

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:04.020
telling a story on a more global scale.

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:09.299
Subbing for Tommy Lee Jones, Will Smith, and
Josh Brolin this time will be Thor: Ragnarok

00:02:09.299 --> 00:02:14.139
co-stars Chris Hemsworth and Tessa Thompson.
They'll be joined in the cast by Emma Thompson,

00:02:14.140 --> 00:02:18.310
no relation, who's returning to her role as
the MiB chief Agent O.

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:22.620
Thanks to their shared screen time in the
Marvel universe, we know the two leads have

00:02:22.629 --> 00:02:28.019
great chemistry. But the movie will reportedly
focus on not just them, but a whole ensemble

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:32.720
of characters, building out the super-secret
organization with a cast of fresh faces. It's

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:38.849
all being brought to life by Fate of the Furious
director F. Gary Gray, who's teased that International

00:02:38.849 --> 00:02:42.459
will take the series to a fresh new place
while still staying true to the movies that

00:02:42.460 --> 00:02:43.300
came before it.

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:48.340
The Men in Black aren't the only cool, calm
and collected characters coming back on June

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:51.180
14. There's also a new movie about Shaft.

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:54.690
"You know, they say that cat Shaft is one
bad mother—"

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:55.660
"Shut up you guys!"

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:57.220
"What's going on?"

00:02:57.220 --> 00:02:58.890
"We're just talking about Shaft."

00:02:58.890 --> 00:03:00.000
"I can dig it."

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:05.010
The film been described as a direct sequel
to the Shaft movie from 2000, which starred

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:09.849
Samuel L. Jackson as John Shaft the Second,
nephew of the original Shaft played by Richard

00:03:09.849 --> 00:03:14.269
Roundtree. In keeping with that tradition,
the new movie will focus on John Shaft the

00:03:14.269 --> 00:03:18.400
Third an FBI agent and cybersecurity expert
played by Jessie T. Usher.

00:03:19.069 --> 00:03:23.379
Both Roundtree and Jackson are making appearances
in the new movie, which will see three generations

00:03:23.379 --> 00:03:28.019
of Shaft teaming up to crack a mystery. It
sounds like more style than one movie can

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:28.520
handle.

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:31.480
"Sty-lin'."

00:03:32.380 --> 00:03:37.219
For American audiences, Shaft will be getting
a full theatrical rollout, but viewers outside

00:03:37.219 --> 00:03:40.379
the country will be able to see it on Netflix
on June 28.

00:03:41.379 --> 00:03:45.549
Thirty-one years after the original Child's
Play first gave him life, Chucky's coming

00:03:45.549 --> 00:03:50.989
back to the big screen on June 21. After seven
movies in the same continuity, the original

00:03:50.989 --> 00:03:55.450
story is finally getting the remake treatment,
this time without the involvement of of creator

00:03:55.450 --> 00:03:59.260
Don Mancini or longtime Chucky voice actor
Brad Dourif.

00:03:59.749 --> 00:04:04.200
On top of a new creative team, the remake
also features a deeply unsettling redesign

00:04:04.209 --> 00:04:09.409
for the series' iconic Good Guys doll, which
will be called a Buddi doll in the new film,

00:04:09.409 --> 00:04:12.960
adding a new level of wide-eyed innocence
to the serial-killer-possessed toy.

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:15.600
"Hi, I'm Chucky. Wanna play?"

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:16.600
"AAAH!"

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:21.859
The Conjuring cinematic universe continues
to grow with a third entry in the Annabelle

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:26.460
series, promising that 2019 will be a banner
year for horror movies about creepy dolls.

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:31.240
The new installment is a follow-up to the
2017 prequel, Annabelle: Creation, and is

00:04:31.241 --> 00:04:36.449
set for release on July 3. The new movie will
bring the series forward in time to The Conjuring

00:04:36.449 --> 00:04:41.199
territory with appearances from Patrick Wilson
and Vera Farmiga's Ed and Lorraine Warren,

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:43.870
who eventually end up in possession of the
haunted doll.

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:45.380
“Where's the doll now?"

00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:47.080
"Someplace safe."

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:51.480
The story for the sequel has been described
as Annabelle meets Night at the Museum. It'll

00:04:52.280 --> 00:04:56.680
feature the haunted doll exerting its twisted
influence inside of the Warrens' cluttered

00:04:56.680 --> 00:05:01.520
artifact room, bringing evil to life to terrorize
the couple's young daughter and her babysitters.

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:06.120
In other words, it's time for the Warrens'
kid to take up the family business of hunting

00:05:06.120 --> 00:05:09.590
demons this summer, whether she's ready for
the job or not.

00:05:10.650 --> 00:05:14.599
Tom Holland's Spider-Man is set to continue
his adventures in the Marvel Cinematic Universe

00:05:14.599 --> 00:05:20.690
with a a second standalone film on July 5,
2019. After taking some detours with the Avengers

00:05:20.690 --> 00:05:24.470
and, uh, getting killed for a little while,
the new movie will take the webslinger back

00:05:24.470 --> 00:05:28.639
to basics with another hit of action-comedy
from the creative team behind Spider-Man:

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:29.140
Homecoming.

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:33.750
Despite the familiarity behind the scenes,
the new Spider-Man adventure will feel different

00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:37.479
from all of the character's previous movies,
taking him outside of his Queens neighborhood

00:05:37.479 --> 00:05:41.900
and across the ocean to Europe. While he's
there, he'll face off with the villainous

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:45.930
Mysterio, a trickster character from Marvel
Comics being brought into live-action for

00:05:45.930 --> 00:05:49.240
the first time, fishbowl and all, by Jake
Gyllenhaal.

00:05:50.020 --> 00:05:54.259
We've all had our share of Uber horror stories:
the driver goes the long way around the city

00:05:54.259 --> 00:05:59.510
to the airport, and you almost miss your flight,
takes one too many back-road "shortcuts" and

00:05:59.510 --> 00:06:03.969
gets completely lost, thus sending you spiraling
into a mini-meltdown in the backseat, or asks

00:06:03.969 --> 00:06:07.570
way too many questions that you weren't prepared
to answer after dancing and drinking the night

00:06:07.570 --> 00:06:12.340
away. It's almost as if the outcome of an
Uber ride is determined by the flip of a coin:

00:06:13.040 --> 00:06:18.860
it's either easy-breezy or kind of a disaster.
In Stuber, it's the latter, only it's the

00:06:18.860 --> 00:06:22.360
driver who's subject to all sorts of unforeseen
troubles.

00:06:22.680 --> 00:06:27.600
Helmed by Future Man and Take Me Home Tonight
director Michael Dowse, Stuber centers on

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:33.229
an unsuspecting Uber driver named Stu, played
by Kumail Nanjiani who picks up his rider,

00:06:33.229 --> 00:06:37.680
Vic, played by Dave Bautista, a detective
who's chasing down a dangerous terrorist.

00:06:38.360 --> 00:06:42.919
Chaos ensues when Stu gets tangled in Vic's
dangerous ordeal, and tries to keep his nerves

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:46.520
level, himself alive, and his coveted five-star
rating intact.

00:06:46.889 --> 00:06:50.300
Accept the ride Stuber is offering when it
hits theaters on July 12.

00:06:51.419 --> 00:06:55.840
Love him or hate him, Quentin Tarantino is
one of the most interesting living filmmakers,

00:06:55.840 --> 00:07:00.409
and he's coming out with a new movie on July
26. After making two straight movies set in

00:07:00.409 --> 00:07:04.469
the old west, Once Upon a Time in Hollywood
is hearkening back to ground the director

00:07:04.469 --> 00:07:08.910
last covered in Pulp Fiction. Once Upon a
Time is still a period piece, though, this

00:07:08.910 --> 00:07:11.800
one set in the wild year of 1969.

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:16.830
The story will focus on an out-of-work TV
actor played by Leonardo DiCaprio, who's looking

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:22.080
to step away from show business. His sidekick
and stunt double Cliff Booth, played by Brad

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:26.330
Pitt, is feeling the same way. Their journey
will intersect somehow with the Manson Family

00:07:26.330 --> 00:07:30.599
murders, with the notorious killings said
to serve as a backdrop of sorts to the main

00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:31.100
story.

00:07:31.160 --> 00:07:35.300
If the concept isn't enticing enough, then
you might be interested in the movie's dazzling

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:40.850
cast. In addition to Pitt, DiCaprio, and Margot
Robbie as the doomed Sharon Tate, the movie

00:07:40.850 --> 00:07:46.409
also features appearances from James Marsden,
Dakota Fanning, Damian Lewis, Timothy Olyphant,

00:07:46.409 --> 00:07:50.941
Burt Reynolds, and Al Pacino, among others.
And that's just a small sample; the movie

00:07:50.941 --> 00:07:56.160
will also feature the return of previous collaborators
Kurt Russell, Michael Madsen, and Tim Roth.

00:07:56.680 --> 00:08:01.140
Tarantino has long contended that he plans
to retire from filmmaking after ten movies.

00:08:01.560 --> 00:08:05.340
Whether that turns out being true or not,
it sounds like movie number nine has everyone

00:08:05.340 --> 00:08:07.080
in Hollywood wanting to be a part of it.

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:13.400
The Fast and the Furious franchise is taking
a year off in 2019, kind of. The summer will

00:08:13.400 --> 00:08:18.110
see the first spinoff in the vehicular mayhem
franchise, this time focusing on Dwayne Johnson

00:08:18.110 --> 00:08:21.749
and Jason Statham's characters, Luke Hobbs
and Deckard Shaw.

00:08:21.749 --> 00:08:26.060
The movie comes from a script from Chris Morgan,
who's been with the franchise since Tokyo

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:30.120
Drift, and promises to team up the two fan-favorite
characters in what sounds like The Odd Couple

00:08:30.120 --> 00:08:35.850
on steroids.The movie is directed by John
Wick and Deadpool 2 helmer David Leitch, which

00:08:35.850 --> 00:08:40.290
has us hoping for both elegant action and
some biting wit. Idris Elba being on board

00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:44.940
to play the movie's main villain is just the
cherry on top. The spinoff kicks off August

00:08:44.940 --> 00:08:46.720
2, and can't get here fast enough.

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:48.820
"Who the hell are you?”

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:50.380
“Bad guy."

00:08:53.080 --> 00:08:57.840
August 2 will also see the release of New
Mutants, a comic book horror hybrid directed

00:08:57.850 --> 00:09:02.500
by Josh Boone. Splintering off from the main
X-Men narrative, New Mutants will introduce

00:09:02.500 --> 00:09:06.830
a group of superpowered teens who are forced
to reconcile their powers and past sins after

00:09:06.830 --> 00:09:09.760
they're captured and held in a mysterious
secret facility.

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:14.720
The new mutants on deck to appear include
Sunspot, who can turn into a ball of dangerous

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:20.380
UV radiation, Mirage, a spooky soothsayer,
and a shape-shifting robot named Warlock.

00:09:20.750 --> 00:09:25.220
The cast includes Maisie Williams from Game
of Thrones, Charlie Heaton from Stranger Things,

00:09:25.220 --> 00:09:28.300
and Anya Taylor-Joy from The Witch, Glass,
and Split.

00:09:28.660 --> 00:09:32.800
The movie has reportedly been through reshoots,
allegedly to both add a whole new character

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:34.420
and make the movie scarier.

00:09:41.020 --> 00:09:44.711
Whatever the real reasons behind the push
back, the film still looks interesting, and

00:09:44.711 --> 00:09:48.700
will hopefully bring something new to the
crowded superhero genre as the summer draws

00:09:48.700 --> 00:09:49.700
to a close.

00:09:50.280 --> 00:09:55.200
Millions of readers around the world are familiar
with Eoin Colfer's Artemis Fowl novels, which

00:09:55.200 --> 00:09:59.600
followed a precocious criminal mastermind
over a series of globetrotting adventures.

00:09:59.910 --> 00:10:03.600
The fantasy series has always seemed ripe
for the big-screen treatment, but for whatever

00:10:03.600 --> 00:10:07.080
reason, an adaptation never took off, until
now.

00:10:07.880 --> 00:10:12.450
Walt Disney's cinematic take on the first
two books is being directed by Kenneth Branagh,

00:10:12.450 --> 00:10:16.760
known to mainstream audiences for his work
directing Thor and Murder on the Orient Express,

00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:21.070
and for that time he showed up in Harry Potter
and the Chamber of Secrets. The lead role

00:10:21.070 --> 00:10:25.810
is set to be played by Irish newcomer Ferdia
Shaw, with Judi Dench playing a gender-swapped

00:10:25.810 --> 00:10:27.620
version of the books' Commander Root.

00:10:28.240 --> 00:10:32.640
With such a beloved book property, the pressure's
on to make fans happy. We'll see if the filmmakers

00:10:32.640 --> 00:10:34.980
pull it off when the movie is released on
August 9.

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:40.520
Check out one of our newest videos right here!
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite

00:10:40.530 --> 00:10:44.640
stuff are coming soon. Subscribe to our YouTube
channel, and hit the bell so you don't miss

00:10:44.640 --> 00:10:45.400
a single one.

